---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="About" description="About weathership — Signals is the federated foundation; Gaius, Ægir, Atelier, Reach, and Vigil are the engines and systems that attach to it.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Signals is the foundation.</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      weathership builds open-source infrastructure for federated
      engines, agents, and data products. Independent projects keep
      their own gRPC, models, and UIs. They attach to
      <a href="/projects/signals/">Signals</a> over a shared protocol,
      scheduler, and warehouse.
    </p>

    <h2>The lattice</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/signals/">Signals</a> — protocol pin
        (<a href="https://github.com/zndx/signals-protocol">signals-protocol</a>),
        YuniKorn, Airflow, Metaflow, Atlas, and transparent hierarchical
        storage (Kudu, Iceberg, Impala, PostgreSQL via impala_fdw).
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/nautilus/">Nautilus</a> — deterministic
        supervisor; one <code>zndx.supervision.v1</code> instance per
        project, scored and promoted independently of the engine.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/gaius/">Gaius</a> — cognition engine; the
        reference peer for protocol shapes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/aegir/">Ægir</a> — instruct; hierarchical
        sequence models for relational metadata.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/atelier/">Atelier</a> — referee; Dempster–Shafer
        classification on a workbench.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/sdg-corpora/">SDG corpora</a> — shared ontology
        those engines train and evaluate against.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/sdg-strategy/">SDG strategy</a> — content-addressed
        record of how a corpus run was made (lens, voices, knobs, targets).
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/reach/">Reach</a> — event-sourced manufacturing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/vigil/">Vigil</a> — resource-oriented fabric
        for high-latency sites.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/zndx/oss-hermes-agent">Hermes Agent</a>
        — agent peer; interactive sessions claim GPUs through Signals.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each project is inspectable in source and documented as it ships.
    </p>

    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      To build durable, transparent infrastructure — systems whose
      behavior is inspectable, whose decisions can be traced, and whose
      failure modes are documented before they're hit. We release as
      open source by default because the systems we want to exist need
      to be reviewable by the people who depend on them.
    </p>

    <h2>Values</h2>
    <dl class="values">
      <dt>Open</dt>
      <dd>
        The software ships under permissive licenses. The architectural
        decisions are written down. The trade-offs we made — and the
        ones we didn't — are visible to anyone who wants to read them.
      </dd>
      <dt>Transparent</dt>
      <dd>
        When we say a system does something, it does that thing. When it
        doesn't, the gap is named. We don't paper over uncertainty with
        confidence we haven't earned.
      </dd>
      <dt>Durable</dt>
      <dd>
        We optimize for the system that's still useful in five years
        over the demo that's compelling next week.
      </dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Origin</h2>
    <p>
      A <em>weather ship</em> was once a vessel stationed in open ocean
      for the express purpose of gathering atmospheric data — a
      floating instrument that turned uncertainty into signal so the
      ships following behind could plan their crossing. Signals plays
      that role for the rest of the fleet.
    </p>
    <p>
      weathership was started by Ryan Hill in 2026 to hold related
      engineering threads under one umbrella. The projects predate the
      umbrella; the umbrella exists because they benefit from being
      held together.
    </p>

    <h2>Press, brand, and assets</h2>
    <p>
      The full <a href="/media-kit/">media kit</a> has the logo (SVG +
      PNG renders), color palette with copyable tokens, type system,
      usage guidelines, and press boilerplate. Everything on this site
      is downloadable.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .prose { max-width: 70ch; }
    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ws-storm);
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 19px;
      color: var(--ws-storm);
    }
    .prose ul { padding-left: 1.2em; }
    .prose li { margin: 0.45em 0; }
    .values { margin: 1em 0 2em; }
    .values dt {
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-top: 1em;
      font-size: 18px;
    }
    .values dd {
      margin: 4px 0 0;
      color: var(--ws-storm);
    }
  </style>
</Base>
